@api = http://localhost:5273

### Register user
POST {{api}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "vendor1", "password": "secret123" }

### Login as user
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "vendor1", "password": "secret123" }

> {% client.global.set("userToken", response.body.token); %}

### Login as admin
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "admin123" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token); %}

### Me
GET {{api}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Create category – no token (expect 401)
POST {{api}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Poisons" }

### Create category – normal user (expect 403)
POST {{api}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Poisons" }

### Create category – admin (expect 201)
POST {{api}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Poisons" }

### ---------- Orders ----------

### Vendor (vendor1) creates a listing
POST {{api}}/api/listings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryId": 1, "title": "Fake Rolex", "description": "Ticks almost like a real one", "price": 10.00, "stock": 50 }

> {% client.global.set("listingId", response.body.id); %}

### Register buyer
POST {{api}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "buyer1", "password": "secret123" }

### Login buyer
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "buyer1", "password": "secret123" }

> {% client.global.set("buyerToken", response.body.token); %}

### Buyer places an order (run 12x → from the 12th order on: discountApplied = true, total 8.00)
POST {{api}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "listingId": {{listingId}}, "quantity": 1 }

### Buying own listing (expect 400)
POST {{api}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "listingId": {{listingId}}, "quantity": 1 }

### My orders (buyer)
GET {{api}}/api/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### My sales (vendor)
GET {{api}}/api/orders/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### FBI demo: start the API with   Fbi__Chance=1 dotnet run --project SatinRoad.Api
### then the next order returns "vendorShutDown": true, the vendor can't log in (403)
### and all their listings disappear from GET /api/listings
GET {{api}}/api/listings
